    result: "0 Years, 9 Months, 7 Days (40 weeks, 280 total days, 6,720 hours)"
commonMistakes:
  - title: "Assuming All Months Have 30 Days"
    description: "Calendar months span 28, 29, 30, or 31 days. Simple division by 30 produces inaccurate fractional days and drifts over multi-year spans."
  - title: "Local Timezone Daylight Saving Shifts"
    description: "Calculating age with local wall-clock midnight can add or subtract an hour during spring and fall clock changes. UTC midnight eliminates this artifact."
  - title: "Leap Day Birthday Ambiguity"
    description: "Individuals born on February 29 do not have that calendar date in common years. Statutory rules vary: UK law observes March 1, while other regions recognize February 28."
  - title: "Misidentifying the Global Age of Majority"
    description: "Full contractual capacity is attained at 18 in over 90% of countries. 21 is specifically the US minimum drinking age and majority in Mississippi and Puerto Rico."
sources:
