    <section style="margin: 2.5rem 0;">
      <h2>How &amp; When to Use the Exact Age Calculator</h2>
      <p>Determining your exact age in days, weeks, and months is essential for several practical, legal, and medical applications:</p>
      <ul style="color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.8; margin-left: 1.25rem;">
        <li><strong>Official Documentation &amp; Visas:</strong> Government passport agencies, border control, and immigration forms often require age verification down to the exact day.</li>
        <li><strong>Pediatric &amp; Infant Milestones:</strong> Pediatric health tracking, vaccine schedules, and developmental stages are measured in weeks and months rather than calendar years.</li>
        <li><strong>School Enrollment Deadlines:</strong> School districts frequently use strict date cutoffs (e.g., must be 5 years old by September 1st) to determine kindergarten eligibility.</li>
        <li><strong>Retirement &amp; Pension Calculations:</strong> Determine the exact day you hit full pension eligibility age (such as 66 or 67 years).</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

